import ../../../testing/driver.dl

class:
    patterns:
        nested event context
    members:
        count as an integer
        child as UI reference

class:
    patterns:
        replacement event context
    members:
        count as an integer
        next as a pointer to integer

to [count scoped action] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    increment the value at (instance's event context as a pointer to integer)

to [count nested action] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set context to instance's event context as a pointer to nested event context
    set target to instance's event target
    increment context's count
    click (context's child) in instance
    require condition (@intrinsic("equal", instance's event context, context as a pointer) and (instance's event target = target)) reporting "Nested activation did not restore its outer callback context."

to [replace scoped action] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set context to instance's event context as a pointer to replacement event context
    set target to instance's event target
    increment context's count
    unbind UI handlers with context (instance's event context) in instance
    bind target in instance to (the function named "count scoped action $") for event 0 with context (context's next as a pointer)

to [count scoped paint] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    set instance to painting's instance
    require condition (instance's event target = (the control labeled "Paint" in instance)) reporting "A paint callback did not receive its target scope."
    increment the value at (instance's event context as a pointer to integer)

appearance paint appearance:
    height is 100

document context example:
    button "One"
    button "Two"
    button "Other"
    surface "Paint" using paint appearance
    code:
        when the "Other" button is clicked:
            require condition @intrinsic("equal", this window's event context, @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)) reporting "An ordinary callback inherited another binding's context."
            increment the value at (this window's state as a pointer to integer)

set application to 7
set instance to an instance of context example with state (the address of application)
set window to the address of instance
set first to the control labeled "One" in window
set second to the control labeled "Two" in window
set inner to 0
set outer to @intrinsic("construct", nested event context, 0, second)
bind second in window to (the function named "count scoped action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of inner) as a pointer)
bind first in window to (the function named "count nested action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of outer) as a pointer)
click first in window
require condition ((outer's count = 1) and (inner = 1)) reporting "Reusable callbacks did not receive their separate binding contexts."
require condition (@intrinsic("equal", instance's event context, @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)) and (instance's event target = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference))) reporting "Activation leaked its context outside dispatch."
unbind UI handlers with context ((the address of outer) as a pointer) in window
unbind UI handlers with context ((the address of inner) as a pointer) in window

# Rebinding one target/event replaces its single callback, including its owner.
set old to 0
set current to 0
bind first in window to (the function named "count scoped action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of old) as a pointer)
bind first in window to (the function named "count scoped action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of current) as a pointer)
unbind UI handlers with context ((the address of old) as a pointer) in window
click first in window
set message to formatted "Rebinding counter results: old={old}, current={current}."
require condition ((old = 0) and (current = 1)) reporting (the data of message)

# Removing the executing binding and adding its replacement affects the next
# activation. The dispatcher must not read a freed handler after its callback.
set replacement to @intrinsic("construct", replacement event context, 0, the address of current)
bind first in window to (the function named "replace scoped action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of replacement) as a pointer)
click first in window
require condition ((replacement's count = 1) and (current = 1)) reporting "Replacing the executing callback invoked its replacement in the same dispatch."
click first in window
require condition (current = 2) reporting "The replacement callback did not run on its next activation."
bind second in window to (the function named "count scoped action $") for event 0 with context ((the address of current) as a pointer)
unbind UI handlers with context (instance's handlers' context) in window
require condition (((the UI handler for first in window for event 0) = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler)) and ((the UI handler for second in window for event 0) = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler))) reporting "Removing bindings through a borrowed owner field lost its context during traversal."
click first in window
require condition (current = 2) reporting "An unbound callback still responded to activation."
click the "Other" button in window
require condition (application = 8) reporting "Callback contexts overwrote the application's own state."

set paints to 0
bind (the control labeled "Paint" in window) in window to (the function named "count scoped paint $") for event 1 with context ((the address of paints) as a pointer)
set view to a UI view of window sized 500 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set surface to the UI layout labeled "Paint" in (view's layout)
require condition ((surface's bounds' width > 0.0) and (surface's bounds' height > 0.0)) reporting "The callback fixture requires a visible paint surface."
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (paints > 0) reporting "The visible paint callback did not run."
require condition @intrinsic("equal", instance's event context, @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)) reporting "Paint dispatch did not restore its callback context."
close the address of view
close window
print line "UI callback contexts nest, replace and remove bindings while preserving application state."
